      "translation": {
        "english_text": "My child! Look at the wonderful gift you have found for your father. Your father must give up country and city alike and go to the forest.",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The father's opening `அப்பா!` is an affectionate/exclamatory address in context; English uses `My child!`."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
