        "page_provenance": [
          {
            "pdf_page": 7,
            "printed_page": 6
          }
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "english_text": "Father! Are you the one speaking like this! Born in a lineage that says spear and sword are companions in life, are you speaking like this! Born in the heroic Pandyan line that declared, `In the pale cruelty of the field of death, the shoulders that sport are our victorious shoulders`, are you speaking like this? He who blinks at the thrust of a spear is a coward! Born of the Tamil who made this his heart-song, are you speaking like this? Shame—disgrace—disgrace to the history of our country itself. The sun that has seen many battlefields will laugh! This earth that bore warriors will laugh. No, Father! Let there be no stain on the history of valour. The land will laugh that Maniballavar, afraid of death, gave his daughter as tribute to the enemy. Let that stain not fall.",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The dense heroic image around `வெண்கொடுமை சாக்காட்டில்` is rendered conservatively and close to its verified wording; the English does not repair the Tamil image."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "maruthanattu-ilavarasi-en-s003-u014",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "status": "verified",
